{"id": "EUVD-2025-210902", "enisaUuid": "223dd1b7-9397-3437-b644-ea0d84fb9287", "description": "libarchive 3.8.x before 3.8.2 has a strcpy heap-based buffer overflow in the gzip writer via the original-filename field to archive_compressor_gzip_open in archive_write_add_filter_gzip.c, aka GHSA-92wx-p669-8gr9. This relates to bsdtar. Exploitation envisions a marginally plausible scenario in which original-filename is obtained from an untrusted party. (original-filename is not derived from the input data.)", "datePublished": "2026-09-14T00:00:00", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-16T14:22:52", "baseScore": 2.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L", "references": ["https://github.com/libarchive/libarchive/pull/2734", "https://github.com/libarchive/libarchive/pull/2734/commits", "https://github.com/libarchive/libarchive/pull/2734/files", "https://github.com/libarchive/libarchive/blob/master/libarchive/archive_write_add_filter_gzip.c", "https://gist.github.com/ttuurrnn/1365a4a9b1c3d5826a3a9bbe111f26b8"], "aliases": ["CVE-2025-64031", "GHSA-pqgv-phc2-5p8r"], "assigner": "mitre", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "8d73473c-982e-3d10-82c8-3053979900e7", "product": {"name": "libarchive", "vendor": {"name": "libarchive"}}, "product_version": "3.8.0 <3.8.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "08085eb7-83ec-39ae-871c-9de866b856bc", "vendor": {"name": "libarchive"}}], "isExploited": false}